WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.805
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.514
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.814 --> 00:00:14.090
Unit five: Money & Shopping. In this unit, you will talk about spending and saving money.

4
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:15.806
Budget.

5
00:00:16.506 --> 00:00:18.842
Budget means a plan for how to spend money.

6
00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:20.700
I make a budget every month.

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.832
Your turn. Say: Budget.

8
00:00:26.532 --> 00:00:27.313
Budget.

9
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.178
Save.

10
00:00:29.878 --> 00:00:31.948
Save means to keep money to use later.

11
00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:34.015
I save some money every week.

12
00:00:34.715 --> 00:00:37.727
Your turn. Say: Save.

13
00:00:40.427 --> 00:00:41.266
Save.

14
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.181
Spend.

15
00:00:43.881 --> 00:00:46.102
Spend means to use money to buy things.

16
00:00:46.402 --> 00:00:48.297
Don't spend all your money at once.

17
00:00:48.997 --> 00:00:51.370
Your turn. Say: Spend.

18
00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:54.955
Spend.

19
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.881
Discount.

20
00:00:57.581 --> 00:01:00.034
Discount means a lower price than usual.

21
00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.426
There's a 20% discount today.

22
00:01:03.126 --> 00:01:05.628
Your turn. Say: Discount.

23
00:01:08.328 --> 00:01:09.247
Discount.

24
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.100
Receipt.

25
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.450
Receipt means a paper that shows what you paid.

26
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.786
Keep the receipt.

27
00:01:16.486 --> 00:01:19.405
Your turn. Say: Receipt.

28
00:01:22.105 --> 00:01:23.025
Receipt.

29
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:24.971
Currency.

30
00:01:25.671 --> 00:01:28.042
Currency means the money used in a country.

31
00:01:28.342 --> 00:01:30.470
The riel is Cambodia's currency.

32
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.019
Your turn. Say: Currency.

33
00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:37.639
Currency.

34
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:39.593
Coupon.

35
00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:43.082
Coupon means a ticket that gives you a lower price.

36
00:01:43.382 --> 00:01:45.591
Use this coupon for free ice cream.

37
00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:49.059
Your turn. Say: Coupon.

38
00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:52.749
Coupon.

39
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.496
Bargain.

40
00:01:55.196 --> 00:01:57.869
Bargain means something bought for a very good price.

41
00:01:58.169 --> 00:02:00.145
This bag was a real bargain.

42
00:02:00.845 --> 00:02:03.335
Your turn. Say: Bargain.

43
00:02:06.035 --> 00:02:06.873
Bargain.

44
00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:08.803
Refund.

45
00:02:09.503 --> 00:02:12.652
Refund means money given back when you return something.

46
00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:14.638
The shop gave me a refund.

47
00:02:15.338 --> 00:02:18.432
Your turn. Say: Refund.

48
00:02:21.132 --> 00:02:21.924
Refund.

49
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:23.941
Cashier.

50
00:02:24.641 --> 00:02:27.314
Cashier means the person who takes your money in a shop.

51
00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.184
Pay the cashier, please.

52
00:02:29.884 --> 00:02:32.803
Your turn. Say: Cashier.

53
00:02:35.503 --> 00:02:36.365
Cashier.

54
00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.165
Warranty.

55
00:02:38.865 --> 00:02:42.072
Warranty means a promise to repair a product if it breaks.

56
00:02:42.372 --> 00:02:44.198
The phone has a one-year warranty.

57
00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:46.958
Your turn. Say: Warranty.

58
00:02:49.658 --> 00:02:50.624
Warranty.

59
00:02:51.617 --> 00:02:52.606
Invoice.

60
00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.281
Invoice means a paper that says how much you must pay.

61
00:02:56.581 --> 00:02:58.546
The shop sent us an invoice.

62
00:02:59.246 --> 00:03:01.817
Your turn. Say: Invoice.

63
00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.402
Invoice.

64
00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:08.474
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:08.774 --> 00:03:11.087
Sreypich, how do you manage your pocket money?

66
00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:14.127
I save a little every week.

67
00:03:15.417 --> 00:03:17.080
Do you spend much on snacks?

68
00:03:18.383 --> 00:03:21.686
Not much. I don't spend many riels on sweets.

69
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:24.530
Do you keep receipts?

70
00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:28.910
Yes! If something breaks, I can get a refund.

71
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:33.458
Grammar focus: Quantifiers (a little and much and many).

72
00:03:33.758 --> 00:03:36.376
I save a little money. I don't spend much.

73
00:03:36.676 --> 00:03:41.415
Use 'much' with things you can't count (money, time) and 'many' with things you can count (snacks, coins).

74
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:44.918
Now read and listen. My Pocket Money.

75
00:03:45.218 --> 00:03:47.926
Every week, I get pocket money from my parents.

76
00:03:49.217 --> 00:03:51.599
I make a budget and try to save a little of it.

77
00:03:52.883 --> 00:03:56.961
I don't spend much money on snacks, and I look for discounts and bargains.

78
00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.540
I always keep the receipt from the cashier.

79
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.976
Once, my headphones broke, and the shop gave me a refund.

80
00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:08.912
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:09.212 --> 00:04:10.759
I don't spend blank money.

82
00:04:11.059 --> 00:04:13.830
A, much. B, many. C, a few.

83
00:04:17.817 --> 00:04:19.317
The answer is A: much.

84
00:04:20.817 --> 00:04:23.048
A paper that shows what you paid is a blank.

85
00:04:23.348 --> 00:04:26.828
A, receipt. B, budget. C, coupon.

86
00:04:30.817 --> 00:04:33.571
The answer is A: receipt.

87
00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:37.907
Money given back when you return something is a blank.

88
00:04:38.207 --> 00:04:42.151
A, refund. B, discount. C, warranty.

89
00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.742
The answer is A: refund.

90
00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.622
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you manage your pocket money?

91
00:04:58.922 --> 00:05:04.396
I save a little money every week, and I don't spend much on snacks. I want to buy a bicycle.

92
00:05:04.696 --> 00:05:06.672
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:07.683 --> 00:05:12.402
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and quantifiers (a little and much and many).

94
00:05:12.702 --> 00:05:17.410
Today's value is saving wisely. Save a little money and spend it carefully.

95
00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.304
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

96
00:05:20.604 --> 00:05:23.581
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

